# No em dashes in client-facing text

Never put an em dash (`—`, U+2014) in anything a player or Thunderstore/GitHub visitor will see. GitHub maps fancy punctuation into listings; Thunderstore descriptions, README, CHANGELOG, wiki, in-game toasts/buttons, and commit messages that land on `main` all count.

Do not use an en dash (`–`, U+2013) as a stand-in either. Use ASCII only: hyphen `-`, comma, period, colon, or parentheses.

```
Bad:  Take All in the pick phase, with curses as the price — plus Nest Egg
Good: Take All in the pick phase, with curses as the price, plus Nest Egg
```

Before a push or Thunderstore publish, search the diff (and `thunderstore.toml` / `manifest.json` `description`) for `—` and `–`. If either is present in client-facing files, replace it before shipping.
